// ProviderCustomization.xcconfig.example
//
// Template for build-time customization values. Copy this file to
// ProviderCustomization.xcconfig (same directory) and fill in the values below,
// then set the Minis target's base configuration to ProviderCustomization.xcconfig
// (Project > Info > Configurations) if it is not already.
//
// Leaving a value empty is allowed for building; the app fails at runtime the
// first time that value is actually needed.

// Only needed to sign in with Claude OAuth credentials (API keys do not need
// it). Requests authenticated with OAuth must open their system prompt with
// the identifying line Claude Code itself sends, or the endpoint rejects
// them. We ship no value — supply your own. Other open-source projects
// talking to the same endpoint declare the same identifier, e.g.
// https://github.com/Wei-Shaw/claude-relay-service
ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_IDENTIFIER_PROMPT =

// ── OAuth clients ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Every provider ships a built-in OAuth client id (and, for the Google-based
// ones, a client secret). To sign in with an OAuth app of your own instead,
// set the matching key below. Each one is injected into the built Info.plist
// as INFOPLIST_KEY_<Name> and read back at runtime.
//
// An empty or unset value keeps the built-in client, so fill in only the
// providers you actually own.
//
// Register the redirect URI your provider expects - the app uses a fixed
// localhost callback: Anthropic http://localhost:54545/callback, Google
// http://localhost:8085/oauth2callback.
//
// AnthropicOAuthClientID =
// OpenAIOAuthClientID =
// XAIOAuthClientID =
// GeminiOAuthClientID =
// GeminiOAuthClientSecret =
// AntigravityOAuthClientID =
// AntigravityOAuthClientSecret =
// CopilotOAuthClientID =
// KimiOAuthClientID =
